---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

/**
 * ⚠️ Have this reviewed by a Colorado attorney before publishing. It is written
 * against carrier requirements and how the service actually runs, but it is not
 * legal advice.
 *
 * Two things carriers specifically look for and that must not be softened:
 *  - the sentence stating mobile opt-in data is never shared for marketing
 *  - a verifiable business name, service area and business-domain email
 */
const updated = 'July 31, 2026';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy | Rocky Mountain Booking"
  description="How Rocky Mountain Booking collects, uses and protects information from callers and client businesses, including mobile opt-in data and review requests."
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  updated={updated}
  intro={`${site.legalName} ("we", "us") provides AI phone answering and appointment booking for service businesses. We are based in ${site.city}, ${site.state} and serve clients throughout the United States. This policy covers two groups: the businesses that subscribe to our service, and the people who call those businesses and reach our assistant.`}
>
  <h2>Information we collect</h2>

  <h3>From callers</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Phone number, name, and service address</li>
    <li>What the call is about, and any appointment details</li>
    <li>A recording and written transcript of the call</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>From client businesses</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Business name, address, and contact details</li>
    <li>Owner and staff names, emails, and mobile numbers</li>
    <li>Hours, service area, pricing and availability you give us</li>
    <li>Calendar access, in order to book appointments</li>
    <li>Billing information, handled by our payment provider</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Call metadata: time, duration, originating number</li>
    <li>Basic website analytics</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      We do not create, extract, store or use voiceprints or any other biometric identifier.
    </strong>{' '}
    Returning callers are recognised by phone number only. There is no voice matching or speaker
    identification of any kind.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not collect Social Security numbers, financial account numbers, health information, or
    government ID numbers. Please do not provide these on a call.
  </p>

  <h2>Mobile information</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>
      No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or
      promotional purposes.
    </strong>{' '}
    Sharing with the service providers described below happens solely to operate the service, and
    those providers are not permitted to use mobile information for their own marketing.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>
      Text messaging originator opt-in data and consent are not shared with any third party.
    </strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    When you tick the optional consent box on our <a href="/contact">contact form</a>, we record the
    time you ticked it and the exact wording that was displayed to you, so there is a record of what
    you agreed to. Full messaging detail is in our <a href="/sms-terms">SMS Terms</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Review requests</h2>
  <p>
    Our Review Bot sends one message after a completed appointment asking the customer to leave a
    review, with a link to the client business&rsquo;s public profile.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Every customer is asked, regardless of how the job went.</strong> We do not survey or
    screen customers to decide who gets asked, we do not send unhappy customers to a private
    feedback form instead, and we never offer discounts, entries, or anything else in exchange for a
    review. Those practices breach Google&rsquo;s review policies and the FTC Consumer Review Rule,
    and we do not build or operate them.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not write, edit, filter, or remove reviews, and we have no control over what a customer
    writes or over the platform they leave it on. Reviews left on Google are governed by
    Google&rsquo;s own terms and privacy policy, not ours.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To answer calls and book appointments for our client businesses</li>
    <li>To send appointment confirmations, reminders and review requests</li>
    <li>To alert business owners to bookings and urgent calls</li>
    <li>To produce call summaries and reporting</li>
    <li>To support, bill, and improve the accuracy of the service</li>
    <li>To meet legal obligations</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not use caller information for our own marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share information with</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>The business you called.</strong> Caller details, appointment information, transcripts
    and recordings are made available to that business, which is responsible for its own handling of
    them.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Service providers</strong> that run parts of the platform on our behalf:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Voice processing and call handling</li>
    <li>Telephony and SMS delivery</li>
    <li>Hosting and data storage</li>
    <li>Payment processing</li>
    <li>Calendar scheduling</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    They may use the information only to provide their service to us, and are bound by their own
    confidentiality and security obligations.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Legal requirements.</strong> Where required by law, subpoena or court order, or to
    protect someone&rsquo;s safety.
  </p>
  <p><strong>Business transfer.</strong> If the business is sold or merged.</p>

  <h2>Call recording</h2>
  <p>
    Calls answered on behalf of a client business may be recorded and transcribed.{' '}
    <strong>Our assistant discloses at the start of every call that it may be recorded</strong>, and
    continuing the call is how consent is given. If you would rather not be recorded, you can end
    the call and contact the business another way.
  </p>
  <p>
    We disclose on every call rather than relying on the rules of any one state. Recording laws
    differ: some states require only one party to consent, and others require every party to. The
    disclosure is made up front in all cases so that recording is consented to wherever the caller
    happens to be.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Call recordings:</strong> 90 days, then deleted</li>
    <li><strong>Transcripts and summaries:</strong> 12 months</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Appointment and contact records:</strong> for the life of our agreement with the client
      business, plus 12 months
    </li>
    <li><strong>Billing records:</strong> as required by tax and accounting law</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    A client business can ask for shorter retention. When an agreement ends, we delete or return
    their data within 7 days on request.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>We honour these rights for everyone, wherever you live.</strong> You can ask us to
    access, correct, delete, or give you a portable copy of your personal data, and you can opt out
    of targeted advertising, the sale of personal data, and profiling. We do none of those last
    three for anyone. To exercise a right, email{' '}
    <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. We respond within the time the law requires,
    and you may appeal a refusal by replying to our response.
  </p>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live these rights may also be guaranteed by law, including the Colorado
    Privacy Act and comparable state privacy laws elsewhere. We do not ask which state you are in
    before honouring a request.
  </p>
  <p>
    Where we process information on behalf of a client business, we act as that business&rsquo;s
    service provider and will pass your request to them and help fulfil it.
  </p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    We use commercially reasonable safeguards including encryption in transit, access controls, and
    restricted administrative access. No system is completely secure and we cannot guarantee
    absolute security.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    The service is for businesses and is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly
    collect their information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy. The date at the top reflects the current version, and material
    changes will be communicated to client businesses directly.
  </p>
</Legal>
